 same commit as `theseus` and `fork/pkt/PKT-0058`, and `git diff` against both is empty.\n- The checkout was still clean after I ran the acceptance command.\n- PKT-0085 was blocked with exactly the same R2 message about the same file. That points to leftover state from another packet in the shared sdkjs checkout, not to this branch. The factory should look at which diff base or commit its scope check used. The rejection message doesn't say, and I couldn't check it from here.\n\n**Results:**\n- `.theseus/oracle/sdkjs-common.sh`: 6/6 suites passed, 10066/10323 assertions, 29 s.\n- `theseus validate`: 0 errors.\n- I added this check to the Executor log and appended the friction line. Validate rejected my first friction line because its format was wrong, so I fixed it in a second commit (`6aa2ad1`, then `07f7832`).\n\n**The diagnosis from the earlier attempt still stands (already in the packet and Atlas):**\n- **color-mods is a test-expectation issue, not a colour bug.** Every failing assertion is off by exactly 1 on one channel. sdkjs uses floating point, while the expected values follow Office's fixed-point rounding.\n- **chartEx-serialize is a broken test page, not a slow run.** The page doesn't load `AllFonts.js`, so it throws while starting up and QUnit never starts. The test also expects a chartEx XML serializer that this codebase doesn't have.\n- **Both suites stay in the oracle's known-broken list.** The fixes are in test files outside the target, so a low-priority request to repair the two test pages is in `.theseus/spawn/`. The chartEx wait dropped from 120 s to 20 s, which brings the oracle run from about 130 s to about 29 s.\n\n**Lessons for the Atlas:**\n- If a QUnit page with `autostart=false` throws before it starts, it looks like a timeout. Hooking `QUnit.log` and `pageerror` shows whether the run hung or was just slow.\n- sdkjs test pages that create `asc_docs_api` need `AllFonts.js` loaded.\n- An R2 rejection should be checked against the sdkjs branch'